From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:27:47 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] kcm_feedback: one Form, data-source programs started
 one by one after the first frame, Provider read once

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). KUserFeedback settings (Global/FeedbackLevel), audit links and the
"--feedback" protocol are unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- The slider is first and labelled "Sharing level:" (was "Plasma:"; alias "Plasma:" in ia/layout.json). The step title
  is a bold label under it, then the intro text as small help text (the two paragraphs merged into one) and the privacy
  policy link. Was: two paragraphs, link, separator, then the form (HIG-001/005, "first thing = main control").
- Noun sections "Information sent" (label "The following will be sent:", or "Nothing is sent." at level 0) and "Sent data"
  (View sent data links; section only when audits exist). Bullet list now wraps. Disabled-centrally InlineMessage stays.
- Relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_feedback.tsv (outer repo). 5 inventory rows kept with ksr markers;
  inventory_check --kcm kcm_feedback --strict: 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code, kcms/feedback/feedback.cpp): the constructor started "plasmashell --feedback" and
"plasma-discover --feedback" together (two heavy binaries competing with the page for CPU) and
feedbackEnabled() built a KUserFeedback::Provider on every read (3 bindings). Now the programs start from a 250 ms
single-shot, one after the other (startNextProgram/finishProgram; a program that fails to start does not stall the
queue), the Provider is read once, and a busy indicator shows in the list after 150 ms (property sourcesLoading).
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: Kirigami.FormData.labelAlignment on a ColumnLayout; the second program's data arrives
about one program run later than before.

